# ctxloom's compiled-in trust root (spec §7, location 1): the public key(s) of
# the ctxloom release / bundle-publishing pipeline. Consumers trust these by
# construction — trusting the ctxloom binary trusts what it ships.
#
# Trusted for the PUBLISH namespace ONLY. The release key signs bundles; it
# cannot approve content on a user's behalf (approval is the user's own key in
# the approve namespace). Keeping publish and approve separate is why a stolen
# publish key cannot forge approvals.
#
# The COMPANION namespace is deliberately absent, even though the same key
# signs the companion binaries ctxloom ships. This store is a union member
# nothing can remove, so a grant written here could never be withdrawn for one
# project. Authorizing a binary to EXECUTE is a decision a project must be able
# to revoke, so `ctxloom init` writes that grant into the project's own
# .ctxloom/allowed_signers (cli.seedCompanionTrust), where deleting the line
# actually withdraws it.
